/*
========================================================================
 REVISION NOTES: BookControllerTest.java (MockMvc + Security Testing)
========================================================================

 GOAL: Controller ko test karna BINA real server chalaye, BINA real
       DB touch kiye, aur security roles (ADMIN/MEMBER) simulate karke.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 1) @WebMvcTest(BookController.class)
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Poori Spring Boot app NAHI chalati (DB, saari Services load
       nahi hoti) - SIRF Web layer (Controller) load karta hai.
    -> FAST test, kyunki DB connect nahi hota.

    ANALOGY: Poora restaurant khol dena vs sirf ek counter test karna.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 2) @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> FAKE HTTP client - Postman jaisa kaam karta hai bina real
       server chalaye.
    -> mockMvc.perform(get("/api/books")) = fake request bhejna


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 3) @MockBean BookService bookService
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Real BookService (jo DB se connect hota) ki jagah
       FAKE/MOCK BookService inject karta hai is test ke liye.
    -> Real DB touch hi nahi hota, tu control karta hai fake
       service kya return karega.


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 4) @Autowired ObjectMapper objectMapper
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> Java object -> JSON string convert karta hai
    -> POST request ki body banane ke kaam aata hai
       (objectMapper.writeValueAsString(newBook))


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 5) @WithMockUser(roles = {"ADMIN", "MEMBER"})
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    -> FAKE LOGIN simulate karta hai.
    -> Bina real JWT token banaye, security-protected endpoint
       test kar sakte hain.
    -> roles = "ADMIN"        -> sirf ADMIN wala fake user
    -> roles = {"ADMIN","MEMBER"} -> dono roles wala fake user
    -> Annotation hi NAHI lagai -> matlab bina login ke request


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 6) Mockito Core Syntax
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    when(bookService.getAllBooks()).thenReturn(list);
    -> "Jab bhi getAllBooks() call ho, real DB query mat karo,
        ye fake list return kar do"

    when(bookService.saveBook(any(Book.class))).thenReturn(newBook);
    -> any(Book.class) = "chahe koi bhi Book object aaye, care
        nahi karna, bas fake newBook return karo"
    -> exact object match karne ki tension nahi leni padti


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 7) mockMvc.perform() + andExpect() Chain
 ------------------------------------------------------------------
    mockMvc.perform(get("/api/books"))          // fake GET request
        .andExpect(status().isOk())              // assert 200
        .andExpect(jsonPath("$[0].title")        // response JSON
                .value("Atomic Habits"));         // ke andar check

    mockMvc.perform(post("/api/books")
            .contentType("application/json")      // body JSON hai
            .content(objectMapper.writeValueAsString(newBook)))
        .andExpect(status().isCreated());         // assert 201

    jsonPath("$[0].title") -> array ke 0th index ka "title" field
    ($  = root, [0] = first item, .title = uska field)


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 8) 4 TEST CASES - SUMMARY TABLE
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    Test                          | User        | Expected | Proves
    ------------------------------|-------------|----------|------------------
    testGetAllBooks_Success       | ADMIN+MEMBER| 200 OK   | Logged-in user
                                   |             |          | data dekh sakta hai
    ------------------------------|-------------|----------|------------------
    testAddBook_AsAdmin_Success   | ADMIN       | 201      | ADMIN add kar
                                   |             | Created  | sakta hai
    ------------------------------|-------------|----------|------------------
    testAddBook_AsMember_Forbidden| MEMBER      | 403      | MEMBER add NAHI
                                   |             | Forbidden| kar sakta -
                                   |             |          | SECURITY PROOF
    ------------------------------|-------------|----------|------------------
    testGetAllBooks_WithoutLogin  | (no login)  | 401      | Bina login
    _Unauthorized                 |             |Unauthoriz| access nahi
                                   |             |ed        | milta


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 JS/JEST ANALOGY (Apna Background Use Karke Yaad Rakh):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    // Jest + Supertest equivalent
    test('GET /api/books returns 200', async () => {
      jest.spyOn(bookService, 'getAllBooks').mockReturnValue([book]);
      const res = await request(app).get('/api/books');
      expect(res.status).toBe(200);
    });

    @MockBean              <->  jest.spyOn().mockReturnValue()
    mockMvc.perform()      <->  request(app).get()
    andExpect()            <->  expect()
    @WithMockUser          <->  fake auth middleware/session inject


 ------------------------------------------------------------------
 GOLDEN RULE (Yaad Rakhne Wali Line):
 ------------------------------------------------------------------

    @WebMvcTest  = sirf Controller layer test (DB/Service real nahi)
    @MockBean    = Service ko FAKE bana do
    @WithMockUser = LOGIN FAKE karo (role ke sath)
    mockMvc      = FAKE Postman (bina real server ke)


